1. Introduction:
Alert management is a critical function in a Security Operations Center (SOC). It involves monitoring, classifying, prioritizing, and responding to security alerts generated by security tools such as SIEM, EDR, and IDS/IPS. Effective alert management helps analysts quickly identify real threats, reduce false positives, and respond to incidents efficiently.
In this task, alert management activities were simulated using Google Sheets, Wazuh, and TheHive to practice alert classification, prioritization, incident ticket creation, and escalation procedures.
2. Objectives:
The main objectives of this exercise were:
To understand the alert handling process in a SOC environment.
To classify alerts based on severity and threat type.
To map alerts to the MITRE ATT&CK framework.
To prioritize alerts using Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) scores.
To document incidents and escalate critical alerts.
3. Tools Used:
3.1 Google Sheets
Used to create an alert classification table and prioritize alerts based on severity and CVSS score.
3.2 Wazuh
An open-source SIEM platform used to monitor and visualize alerts through dashboards.
3.3 The Hive
A security incident response platform used for creating and managing incident tickets.
